{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.borromean_1dim_blocks_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.borromean_1dim_blocks_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L109-L115","doc":"Both 1-dim block characters of the Borromean baryon are pinned to `1` — the\ngeneration hierarchy provably cannot come from these blocks' ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L104-L107","doc":"The **Borromean baryon** $(\\sigma_1\\sigma_2^{-1})^3$ has writhe `0`: three\npositive `σ₁` (letter `1`) and three negative `σ₂⁻¹` (letter `-2`). Concrete,\ndecidable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_sign_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_sign_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L99-L102","doc":"Likewise the sign block collapses to `1` at writhe 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_trivial_writhe_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_trivial_writhe_zero","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L92-L97","doc":"**The prune.** On a writhe-balanced braid (`writhe w = 0`) the trivial-block\ncharacter collapses to `1`, independent of `q`: a balanced baryon braid carries\nno generation information in its trivial block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_sign_eq_negqinv_zpow_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_sign_eq_negqinv_zpow_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L82-L90","doc":"**Sign-block character is a writhe monomial:** `χ_sign(β) = (-q⁻¹) ^ writhe(β)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_trivial_eq_q_zpow_writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chi_trivial_eq_q_zpow_writhe","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L71-L80","doc":"**Trivial-block character is a writhe monomial:** `χ_triv(β) = q ^ writhe(β)`.\nThe falsifiable content — a 1-dim block sees *only* the writhe, not the braid's\ninternal structure. Proved by list induction + `zpow_add₀` (needs `q ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe_cons","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L67-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe_nil","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chiSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chiSign","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L60-L63","doc":"Character of the **sign** ($[1^n]$) 1-dim Hecke block on a braid word:\neach generator maps to the second Hecke eigenvalue `-q⁻¹`, so the letter\ncontributes `(-q⁻¹) ^ sign`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chiTrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.chiTrivial","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L56-L58","doc":"Character of the **trivial** ($[n]$) 1-dim Hecke block on a braid word:\neach positive crossing contributes `q`, each negative `q⁻¹` (= `q ^ sign`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TrivialBlockWrithe.writhe","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TrivialBlockWrithe.lean#L53-L54","doc":"Writhe of a braid word = sum of the crossing signs. ","signatureChunk":0}]}